  "body": "Found by the post-merge review of PR #1058 (merged 2026-11-12).\n\n`crates/app/src/project/validate.rs` (about lines 147-148) refuses a project whose tool has unusable parameters with \"tool parameters are not usable: ToolDto { ...the whole struct printed... }\". The refusal is right (the review's load test refused all 15 bad `turning` values: surface speed 0, negative or absurd; feed 0 or negative; max rpm 0, negative or below the tool's rpm; a missing or unknown field), but the message does not say which tool or which field, and prints a debug dump.\n\nDone means: the message names the tool and the failing field in plain English, for example \"tool 'T1': turning surface speed 0 is outside 1..2000 m/min\"; pinned by a test for a turning field and for one milling field.",
